# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Qianyu Zheng et al. (2026). Improving Reliability of Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials with Physics-Informed Pretraining.
#   Journal of Chemical Information and Modeling. doi:10.1021/acs.jcim.6c00826  arXiv:2602.19592v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2602.19592v1 (sha256 c8d75eb1f1e60043...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 97 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the comparison of Table 2: CGCNN, TorchMD-NET and
# M3GNet trained on a silica, a phosphorus and an MPtrj (Li-Mn-O-P) data
# set under three training strategies (baseline, sharpness-aware
# minimisation, and the paper's pretraining on data labelled by a fitted
# EAM potential followed by fine-tuning): 24 runs with energy, force and
# stress MAEs.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
